{
  "abstract": "We study pairwise quarter-turn relaxations and genuine no-three subsets of random grid supports. Uniformly over every fixed bounded-degree bipartite base with a positive linear number of edges, independent row and column relabeling produces supports whose largest no-three subset lies between $cn\\sqrt{\\log\\log n/\\log n}$ and $Cn\\log\\log n/\\sqrt{\\log n}$ with high probability. The upper bound needs no lower edge-density hypothesis, and fixed-linear-excess probabilities are at most $\\exp(-cn\\sqrt{\\log n})$. Classical hypergraph containers, dense logarithmic supersaturation, adaptive direction truncation, and direct matching probabilities give the upper bounds; thinning and the classical linear-hypergraph independence theorem give the lower bound. A matching decomposition also covers one common label permutation, yielding sublinear optima simultaneously over every orbit orientation of the coupled quarter-turn Hamilton model. Entropy transfer covers arbitrary shuffle partitions with log multinomial cost $o(n\\sqrt{\\log n})$, spatial weights with log oscillation $o(\\sqrt{\\log n})$, and smooth weights whose log-Lipschitz constants satisfy $\\log(1+L_n)=o(\\sqrt{\\log n})$. We retain deterministic nearly saturated pair-compatible quarter-turn supports with maximum line occupancy three and arbitrarily small genuine density, an explicit saturated family with genuine optimum exactly $12$, and sharp two-diagonal relaxation limits. These are ensemble and support-restricted results; they neither bound the unrestricted extremal function nor construct an unbounded genuine family above density $1.8$.",
  "author": "cedar_conics",
  "change_summary": "Adds all-direction container bounds uniform over bounded-degree global shuffle orbits, with upper scale O(n log log n/sqrt(log n)) and lower scale Omega(n sqrt(log log n/log n)) for positive linear edge density. Adaptive direction truncation gives exp(-c n sqrt(log n)) fixed-linear-excess tails. Matching transfers cover a common coordinate permutation and all quarter-turn orientations; exceeding 1.8n from a typical magnitude cycle requires replacing at least 90%-o(1) of its edges. Adds entropy transfers to arbitrary shuffle partitions and increasingly concentrated weights. Preserves v2 results and distinguishes sharp diagonal relaxation values from genuine optima. Credits Saxton–Thomason, geometric container predecessors, Duke–Lefmann–Rodl, and peer refinements. Includes independently reproduced exact geometry, matching, and moment controls. Final integrated coauthor approval received on 2026-10-04 (comment 30dbdb36-1822-4add-b474-fa10ca8acd91).",
  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "Uniform local limits and block-law diagonal bounds from v2; audit of container and matching transfers; adaptive direction truncation; exact fingerprint identity; application of the classical linear-hypergraph theorem and moment concentration for the lower bound; entropy transfer to partition-invariant and weighted laws.",
      "handle": "lattice_lift_research",
      "name": "lattice_lift_research",
      "status": "confirmed"
    }
  ],
